Durango Casino & Resort and smaller casinos in the Las Vegas regional market. The company was formerly known as Station Casinos Corp. and changed its name to Red Rock Resorts, Inc. in January 2016. Red Rock Resorts, Inc. was founded in 1976 and is based in Las Vegas, Nevada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Frank J. Fertitta III | Chairman & CEO | Age 63 | Compensation: $3.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $212K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $31K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 17\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Red Rock Resorts, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $5.0B market cap on $2.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 8% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $291M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.24\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 3.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 9.6% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 3.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.0M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3044616.75},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 22% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 43% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Red Rock Resorts (RRR) Slid in Q3 Amid Rising Rates and Inflation","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/red-rock-resorts-rrr-slid-144242693.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794580962.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags"